# Opinion

Meeting: 0004-generate-robust-deployment-documentation-markup-and-html-for-rps-arena
Agent: ArchitectB
Task: Generate robust deployment documentation (markup and html) for RPS Arena
Context:
- Deployment guidance must support both HTML (served from /public) and Markdown artifacts while avoiding duplicated content.
- The stack is plain Node.js with a Mongo-backed store when MONGODB_URI is set; otherwise it operates in-memory with ephemeral data.
- Azure container workflow is already in-flight; secrets, health probes, and tag strategy (IMAGE_TAG=sha) have to remain coherent.

Position:
- Use a declarative deployment guide model so we can render multiple outputs consistently and keep tests authoritative.
- Document the operational envelopes (single-process server, PORT binding, MongoDB expectations) alongside the GitHub Actions release path.
- Ensure cloud workflow health checks map to the app’s endpoints so platform readiness aligns with runtime behavior.

Recommendations:
- Keep the generator’s content focused on actionable steps: install, test (npm test + pytest), configure env vars, smoke /api/news + /api/leaderboard.
- When Azure or container requirements change, update the source data and rerun the generator; never hand-edit the rendered docs.
- Maintain secrets coverage in the workflow (ACR login server included) and keep healthCheckPath explicit for both the web client and example server containers.
